@startuml AD-01-weekly-roster
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor white
 BorderColor black
 DiamondBackgroundColor white
 DiamondBorderColor black
 StartColor black
 EndColor black
}
skinparam swimlaneBorderColor black
skinparam swimlaneTitleFontStyle bold
skinparam conditionStyle InsideDiamond
skinparam wrapWidth 260
skinparam dpi 180
title AD-01: Weekly Roster Preparation and Publishing
' Traces: UC-07, UC-08, UC-13, UC-15; FR-30/32/33/41-46/49-51/53/71.
' Sources: DEC-09, DEC-10, DEC-16, DEC-19, DEC-31, DEC-32, DEC-39, DEC-43, DEC-45, DEC-46.
' SMS chosen by user on 2026-10-03. Detailed guards and exceptions remain in UC-07.
|Manager|
start
:Open Planning Week or
current / future Published week;
|System|
:Show Availability, Workload,
Vans and Unassigned Jobs;
|Manager|
repeat
:Prepare Crew / Standby / Job changes,
or choose Publish;
if (Compare Staff?) then (yes)
  :Compare up to three Staff (UC-08);
else (no)
endif
|System|
:Check authority and blocking rules;
if (Blocking error?) then (yes)
 :Explain error; retain roster;
else (no)
 :Show Workload and warnings;
 |Manager|
 :Confirm change and warning overrides;
 |System|
 :Save change / publication
and audit successful changes;
 if (Save successful?) then (yes)
  :Notify Staff for Published events (UC-15)\nKeep Draft hidden from Staff;
 else (no)
  :Retain previous roster
and show retry / support advice;
 endif
endif
|Manager|
repeat while (More roster actions?) is (yes) not (no)
|System|
if (Roster status?) then (Draft)
 |Manager|
 :Review saved Draft;
else (Published)
 |Staff|
 :View Assignments, Standby
and Workload (UC-13);
endif
stop
legend bottom
Planning starts Thursday; normal publication is Monday before the Planning Week.
Standby must be Available all day and outside every Crew; missing cover only warns.
Notifications: Landing Page, email and SMS. Save failures: up to 3 retries, then retry / IT Administrator.
endlegend
@enduml
